+### §viewport-media-query — the shell's layout step follows the viewport width
+- Since: 2026-10-23
+- Supersedes: §container-not-viewport (2026-09-15), overridden by the maintainer.
+- Decision: the shell's layout step uses a viewport media query, `@media (min-width: 720px)`.
+- Previously: the layout steps used `@container` queries on `.shell`, so the shell responded to its own width. That
+  was adopted because the shell renders inside split panes as narrow as 380px on a 1440px screen, where viewport
+  queries picked the two-column layout and clipped the sidebar (incident 2026-09-14).
+- Known consequence: inside a narrow split pane on a wide screen the two-column layout is selected again, so the
+  sidebar can clip as it did in incident 2026-09-14. The maintainer accepted this trade-off.
